WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 3: Fun and Games.

2
00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:12.460
In this unit, your child learns the words for games and
play — action words like bounce, roll, throw and catch.

3
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:20.160
They learn the names of parts of the body, and words that
say where things are (on, under, next to), and left and right.

4
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:25.600
They play simple games, learn a game from
another country, and listen to a funny story.

5
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.960
Along the way they hear the short 'u' sound (sun, fun, duck).

6
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:34.260
The goal is happy, active English — learning through play.

7
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:39.800
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:47.360
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name and
act out ball actions (bounce, roll, throw, catch, hit).

9
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:52.040
you will also name parts of the body
(hand, foot, ear, nose, shoulder, head…).

10
00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:57.940
you will also say where something is (on,
under, next to) and show left and right.

11
00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.540
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

12
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:07.180
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: bounce, roll, throw, catch, hit, run.

13
00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:12.360
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

14
00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:15.780
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

15
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:21.060
The reading sequence includes Amal and
the Big Ball and Talk about Fun and Games.

16
00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.520
Read actively.

17
00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:27.460
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

18
00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.380
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

19
00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.160
The first language focus is Language pattern 1.

20
00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:40.380
Listen to the model, point to the matching
picture, then say the pattern: I can ___.

21
00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:48.740
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

22
00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:53.180
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

23
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.520
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

24
00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:01.100
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

25
00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:04.640
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

26
00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:06.080
You are ready to begin.

27
00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:12.140
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

28
00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.900
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

29
00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:20.860
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
